      "claim": "Stream velocity is the primary determinant of a stream's competence (maximum particle size) and capacity (total sediment load).",
      "evidence": "Hydraulic principles and the Hjulström curve demonstrate that higher flow velocity provides greater shear stress and turbulence, allowing the transport of larger and more numerous particles.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": []
